    "title": "Add a look from a library",
  },
  {
    "description": "Define or change a material of the design, for walls' finishes (wall_update finish), floors (space_update floor) and looks. Start from an existing material (from: its id, keeping its pattern, sizes and texture) and change what differs; a new id adds a material, an existing id of the design changes it everywhere it is used, and a default material id makes a version of it for this design only. texture: a photographed texture set laid at its real size and tinted to the colour (stucco cement concrete brick laminate oak walnut plywood terracotta paving granite terrazzo gravel grass marble rubble planks soil bark jersey linen velvet clay), or null for a plain colour. Default materials: fabric cushion linen bedding canvas canvas2 wood woodDark birch white red cabinet countertop ceramic ceramicShade appliance plaster stone stoneDark terracotta soil iron dark glass book1 book2 book3 book4 flower tube bark leaf leaf2 carBody carGlass tyre metal headlight taillight frame glassBlock wall water grate oak teak tile antislip redtile paver terrazzo gravel cement marble slate grass paint greybrick redbrick stonewall woodcladding concrete.",
    "examples": [
      {
        "input": {
          "color": "#e8dfcf",
          "from": "paint",
          "id": "limewash",
          "name": "米白石灰墙",
        },
        "note": "A warm off-white wall finish",
      },
      {
        "input": {
          "color": "#7d8186",
          "from": "stonewall",
          "id": "greystone",
          "name": "青灰毛石",
          "texture": "rubble",
        },
        "note": "Grey rubble stone",
      },
    ],
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "color": {
          "description": "Its colour as CSS hex (sRGB), e.g. #d9cbb5",
          "pattern": "^#([0-9a-fA-F]{3}|[0-9a-fA-F]{6})$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "from": {
          "description": "An existing material to start from",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "id": {
          "description": "Material id",
          "maxLength": 64,
          "pattern": "^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "name": {
          "description": "Its name, in the language the project data uses",
          "maxLength": 200,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "roughness": {
          "description": "0 polished … 1 matt",
          "maximum": 1,
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": "number",
        },
        "texture": {
          "description": "A texture set id, or null for none",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null",
          ],
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "kind": "edit",
    "name": "material_define",
    "permission": "reversible",
    "runtime": "any",
    "title": "Define a material",
  },
  {
    "description": "Customise one piece of furniture, door or window, or element without changing its look: set values for the parameters its look declares (materials of its main surfaces, decoration on/off, shape choices…; look_get with its target lists them with their defaults). null puts a parameter back to the look's default; reset clears all. Values are checked against the declarations (type, enum, range; a material must exist), then by building the object with them. To change many objects, call it for each one that should change.",
    "examples": [],
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "object": {
          "description": "ID or name of a piece of furniture, door or window, or element",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "params": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "maxLength": 200,
                "type": "string",
              },
              {
                "type": "number",
              },
              {
                "type": "boolean",
              },
              {
                "type": "null",
              },
            ],
          },
          "default": {},
          "description": "Parameter → value (null: back to the default)",
          "propertyNames": {
            "type": "string",
          },
          "type": "object",
        },
        "reset": {
          "default": false,
          "description": "Clear all values first",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "object",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "kind": "edit",
    "name": "params_set",
    "permission": "reversible",
    "runtime": "any",
    "title": "Set look parameters",
  },
  {
    "description": "Add a new furniture type to the design (a fish tank, a mahjong table…), with its default size and, optionally, a recipe for its look (format in look_add). Then place it with furniture_add.",
