  },
  {
    "description": "The modules this design adds to its canvas page (id, name, description, version, size) and which keep data. sources=true also returns their source, to change one with canvas_module_put.",
    "examples": [],
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "sources": {
          "type": "boolean",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "kind": "query",
    "name": "canvas_modules",
    "permission": "read",
    "runtime": "any",
    "title": "List canvas modules",
  },
  {
    "description": "Add a module to this design's canvas page, or replace one (same id; its version goes up). The canvas is a sandboxed web page drawn from ready-made code, the wheels; a module is an ES module run on top of the default page: \`export default function (canvas) { … }\`. Read canvas_wheels first and use the wheels (plan layers, selectable, draggable, snap lines, the wall tool, data) rather than rewriting them. One module per feature, a few hundred lines at most. The page has no network. The module is tried in the open page before it is saved: an error comes back to fix; otherwise the result says what it put on the page (drawn: elements by tag, texts, buttons, snaps). Keep the module's own state with canvas.data.set (canvas_data_set), so it undoes and is shared with the design.",
    "examples": [],
    "input": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "properties": {
        "description": {
          "description": "What it does (English)",
          "maxLength": 1000,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "id": {
          "description": "kebab-case id, e.g. structural-grid",
          "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,47}$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "name": {
          "description": "Display name, in the language the project data uses",
          "maxLength": 80,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "origin": {
          "description": "When importing a wheel: the origin canvas_wheel_get returned, passed as is (drop it when you change the source)",
          "properties": {
            "library": {
              "maxLength": 64,
              "type": "string",
            },
            "module": {
              "maxLength": 64,
              "type": "string",
            },
            "version": {
              "maximum": 9007199254740991,
              "minimum": 1,
              "type": "integer",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "library",
            "module",
            "version",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "source": {
          "description": "The module source",
          "maxLength": 60000,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "name",
        "source",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "kind": "edit",
    "name": "canvas_module_put",
    "permission": "reversible",
    "runtime": "any",
    "title": "Save canvas module",
  },
  {
    "description": "Remove a module from this design's canvas page, with the data it kept.",
